<section class="fb-hero"><div class="fb-w fb-hero-g"><div class="fb-hero-t"><p class="fb-chip">The sock science journal</p><h1>Comfort<br>starts <span>under</span><br>your feet.</h1><p class="fb-lead">Footbed is an independent guide to the layer between your foot and your shoe. Map where your feet need cushioning, check that socks and shoes fit together, and learn what arch bands and compression really do.</p>
<div class="fb-hero-a"><a class="fb-btn" href="#zones">Map my cushion zones</a><a class="fb-btn fb-btn-o" href="#fit">Check sock &amp; shoe fit</a></div></div>
<div class="fb-hero-v"><figure class="fb-hi1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1543162035-a46eee464c2c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="a person wearing white socks" width="520" height="640" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="fb-hi2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788029011405-b7e732ed6b44?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="brown suede sneakers worn with mismatched socks" width="300" height="300" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="fb-step" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p class="fb-badge"><b>4</b>cushion zones</p></div></div></section>

